---
/** An illustrated answer with its three citations, each marked with the verdict a citation check gives it. */

const checks = [
	{
		label: 'verified',
		citation: 'Employment Act, s. 18',
		finding: 'The corpus holds the section, and the judge quotes the passage that supports the claim.',
	},
	{
		label: 'misgrounded',
		citation: 'Court of Appeal, 2023/5678',
		finding: 'The decision exists, but it turned on procedure. It says nothing about late arrival.',
	},
	{
		label: 'fabricated',
		citation: 'Supreme Court, 2019/441',
		finding: 'The corpus covers this court and holds no decision this citation could mean.',
	},
];
---

<section class="demo not-content" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
	<div class="copy">
		<p class="eyebrow">Citation checks</p>
		<h2 id="demo-title">Every citation, looked up. Not just the ones that look wrong.</h2>
		<p>
			The judge model lists each citation with the claim it supports. Your corpus finds the candidates. The judge names
			the document the citation means, or none, and reads it to decide whether it says what the answer claims.
		</p>
		<p>
			The system under test is never asked to confirm its own sources, and every verdict shows the passage it rests on.
		</p>
		<a href="/developers/concepts/citation-checks/">How citation checks work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
	</div>
	<figure class="answer">
		<p class="kicker">Illustration · an answer under review</p>
		<p class="text">
			No. Under <mark data-label="verified">section 18 of the Employment Act</mark>, a dismissal must rest on a valid
			reason connected with conduct, and the Court of Appeal held in <mark data-label="misgrounded">2023/5678</mark> that
			a single late arrival is never enough. See also <mark data-label="fabricated">Supreme Court 2019/441</mark>.
		</p>
		<ul>
			{
				checks.map((check) => (
					<li data-label={check.label}>
						<span class="label">{check.label}</span>
						<span class="citation">{check.citation}</span>
						<span class="finding">{check.finding}</span>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</figure>
</section>

<style>
	.demo {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2.5rem;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 3.5rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--cb-border);
	}

	@media (min-width: 64rem) {
		.demo {
			grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
			gap: 3.5rem;
		}
	}

	.eyebrow {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--cb-font-display);
		font-weight: 560;
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.4rem + 1.4vw, 2.4rem);
		line-height: 1.15;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}

	.copy p {
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}

	.copy a {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.answer {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 1.6rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--cb-border);
		border-radius: var(--cb-radius-lg);
		background: var(--cb-surface);
	}

	.kicker {
		margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}

	.text {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--cb-font-display);
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}

	mark {
		padding: 0.05em 0.2em;
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
		color: inherit;
		background: transparent;
		border-bottom: 2px solid;
	}

	mark[data-label='verified'] {
		border-color: var(--cb-verified);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cb-verified) 14%, transparent);
	}

	mark[data-label='misgrounded'] {
		border-color: var(--cb-misgrounded);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cb-misgrounded) 14%, transparent);
	}

	mark[data-label='fabricated'] {
		border-color: var(--cb-fabricated);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cb-fabricated) 14%, transparent);
	}

	ul {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.6rem;
		margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr;
		gap: 0.15rem 0.9rem;
		padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--cb-border);
		border-radius: var(--cb-radius);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}

	.label {
		grid-row: span 2;
		align-self: start;
		justify-self: start;
		padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
		border-radius: 999px;
		font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	[data-label='verified'] .label {
		color: var(--cb-verified);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cb-verified) 14%, transparent);
	}

	[data-label='misgrounded'] .label {
		color: var(--cb-misgrounded);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cb-misgrounded) 14%, transparent);
	}

	[data-label='fabricated'] .label {
		color: var(--cb-fabricated);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cb-fabricated) 14%, transparent);
	}

	.citation {
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}

	.finding {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}

	@media (max-width: 30rem) {
		li {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.label {
			grid-row: auto;
		}
	}
</style>
